dialect protocol
protocol stdio.gif.89a.diff
version 1
schema stdio.gif.89a.diff
start diff

# Real binary diff-frame `protocol::DiffCodec::encode_diff`/`decode_diff` NOW emit for
# `GifDiff` (89a) — upgraded, this program (P2-FG2), from the F6-era
# `print_diff().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut (see this artifact's report; the FG1
# wave's own closer report flagged leaving this un-upgraded as a real defect to not repeat).
# `GifDiff` is a STRUCT with a mix of PLAIN `Option<T>` fields (`width`/`height`/
# `background_color_index`/`pixel_aspect_ratio`/`frames`/`comments`/`app_extensions`) and TWO
# TRI-STATE `Option<Option<T>>` fields (`gct`, `loop_count`) — same 2-way/3-way flag-per-field
# design as 87a's own sibling protocol file and PNG's own precedent (avoids
# `protocol-cond-cannot-chain`, see that file's own doc comment for the full rationale).
#
# `loop_count` is FIXED-width (`u16`, matching `GifSnapshot::loop_count`'s own on-disk NETSCAPE
# loop-count width) so its tri-state value is a plain conditional field, no length prefix
# needed — same treatment PNG's own `gama`/`chrm` (fixed-width tri-state) fields get. `gct`
# (variable-length: a Vec of RGB triples), `frames`/`comments`/`app_extensions` (the
# `removed`/`modified`/`added` collection triples, recursively nesting `GifFrame`/
# `GifFrameDiff`/`GifPlainText`/`GifAppExtension`/`String` values) are all length-prefixed
# opaque byte blobs (`<name>_len varint` + `Array(u8, Field(<name>_len))`) — `Prim::Ref` to a
# struct/enum still unconditionally errors at walk time (confirmed unchanged since P2-M2,
# `protocol-prim-ref-recursion`), so their own internal shape isn't further protocol-walkable;
# the Rust `encode_diff`/`decode_diff` side (`../🦀️.rs`'s `RealBinaryDiffFrame`/
# `RealBinaryPrimitives` regions) IS genuinely, fully structured real binary (real varint
# counts, real per-item recursive encoding, incl. `GifFrameDiff`'s own THREE nested tri-state
# fields — `lct`/`transparent_index`/`plain_text`) — this is purely a limit on how deep the
# PROTOCOL DESCRIPTION itself can validate structurally, same documented limitation as every
# other stdio pilot's own nested-payload field.
framing record

field width_flag u8
field width_value u32 if width_flag eq 1
field height_flag u8
field height_value u32 if height_flag eq 1

field gct_flag u8
field gct_len varint if gct_flag eq 2
field gct_value Array(u8, Field(gct_len)) if gct_flag eq 2

field background_color_index_flag u8
field background_color_index_value u8 if background_color_index_flag eq 1
field pixel_aspect_ratio_flag u8
field pixel_aspect_ratio_value u8 if pixel_aspect_ratio_flag eq 1

field loop_count_flag u8
field loop_count_value u16 if loop_count_flag eq 2

field frames_flag u8
field frames_len varint if frames_flag eq 1
field frames_value Array(u8, Field(frames_len)) if frames_flag eq 1

field comments_flag u8
field comments_len varint if comments_flag eq 1
field comments_value Array(u8, Field(comments_len)) if comments_flag eq 1

field app_extensions_flag u8
field app_extensions_len varint if app_extensions_flag eq 1
field app_extensions_value Array(u8, Field(app_extensions_len)) if app_extensions_flag eq 1
